    "note": "An **alternative** is something you could choose instead of what was already named: *an alternative to driving*. An **option** is any one of the possible choices: *We have three options*. A **choice** can also mean the act or right of choosing: *It's your choice*."
  },
  "usage_note": "Some careful writers use **alternative** only when there are exactly two choices, but most people use it for any number.",
